ng about the second coming of  Christ or whatever there's a  then we get to the cherry on top judge  Jeanine actually brings on a protester  this is a protester from Michigan and  praises the protester I guess for  putting people at risk of infection take  a look  Denny dent Dingell who is the pitcher  senator didn't have nice things to say  about you guys and I was rather shocked  here she is a representative of your  state criticizing this this peaceful  protest and it was pre Tempe SFIL saying  it was inexcusable what water Michigan's  reaction to her well I can tell you look  at Michigan look the nation what we've  done with operation gridlock and has  ignited a fire that has spread across  this entire nation Arizona Pennsylvania  Texas I mean today New York great  example of gridlock people rising up all  across this nation all right and you  know a lot of people are very proud of  you Michonne and what you've done and  let me just say Debbie Dingell is a  congresswoman and not a senator of  course the issue isn't whether it was a  peaceful protest again they are just  completely changing the parameters of  the discussion the peaceful nature of  the protest isn't an issue the public  health risk of the protest is what's at  issue they called it operation gridlock  they are grid locking streets and  preventing patients who need care from  getting to hospitals and this is how the  echo chamber works we're seeing it  happen in real time  Trump tweets about liber8 Michigan  liber8 Minnesota whatever Trump says  protesters are being responsible even  when they're not and then judge Jeanine  brings on a protester and acts like  they're doing some amazing principled  thing when all they're doing is putting  people at risk of getting the virus and  compromising the long-term economic  stability of the country remember  they're insisting that in the short term  opening will be good economically maybe  it will maybe it won't but what we know  from the 19  flu pandemic is